        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-08-31 01:43:44.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-17000 osd-ldiskfs: name the device in the osd_ro() message",
        "message": "LU-17000 osd-ldiskfs: name the device in the osd_ro() message\n\nosd_ro() prints sb->s_bdev with %lx.  The cast does match the\nspecifier, but a raw kernel pointer tells an admin nothing and bypasses\nthe %p hashing.  Print od_mntdev instead, which osd_mount() fills in\nwith the same device path its own messages name and which the mntdev\nsysfs attribute reports.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I9b8c6419fef793ee965187230d57e98abcd9ae34\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
